ders? J Gen Intern Med. 1999;14:409&#x02013;17. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10417598</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fernandez</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Schillinger</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Grumbach</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenthal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Perez-Stable</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physician language ability and cultural competence. An exploratory study of communication with Spanish-speaking patients</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>167</fpage><lpage>174</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1525-1497.2004.30266.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Fernandez A, Schillinger D, Grumbach K, Rosenthal A, Stewart AL, Wang F, Perez-Stable EJ. Physician language ability and cultural competence. An exploratory study of communication with Spanish-speaking patients. J Gen Intern Med. 2004;19:167&#x02013;74. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15009796</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Parker</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>MV</given-names></name><name><surname>Coates</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name><name><surname>Pitkin</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use and effectiveness of interpreters in an emergency department</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>1996</year